        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Before the conflict began, inflation was at 2.4%, but the closure of the strait of Hormuz has affected energy prices</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump\">Donald Trump</a> said “I love the inflation” after new data showed that <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/inflation\">inflation</a> jumped to an annual rate of 4.2% in May, the third consecutive monthly increase since the start of the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/us-israel-war-on-iran\">Iran war</a> and a three-year high.</p><p>Speaking from the White House on Wednesday, the US president <a href=\"https://x.com/Acyn/status/2064741127249690894\">said</a> that he was not concerned about inflation because of recent developments in the conflict.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/jun/10/inflation-report-rate\">Continue reading...</a>"
